WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.515
Private retrieval-augmented generation is an architecture pattern for grounding AI responses in controlled source material.

00:00:05.515 --> 00:00:09.847
Instead of relying only on what a model already learned during training,

00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:13.819
the system retrieves documents, policies, procedures, tickets, product notes, code guidance,

00:00:13.819 --> 00:00:18.512
or other approved knowledge and provides that material as context for the answer.

00:00:18.512 --> 00:00:22.483
The private part adds requirements that a simple demonstration may ignore.

00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:26.815
A demo can upload a few files and return a plausible response.

00:00:26.815 --> 00:00:30.786
A production private RAG system has to preserve source ownership, classification,

00:00:30.786 --> 00:00:34.036
ingestion date, access rules, tenant boundaries, freshness, citations, logging,

00:00:34.036 --> 00:00:35.841
deletion expectations, and operational support.

00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:39.451
RAG does not make information automatically correct or automatically authorized.

00:00:39.451 --> 00:00:42.700
Retrieved material is evidence for the model to consider,

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.866
not an unlimited source of authority.

00:00:44.866 --> 00:00:49.198
The architecture still needs rules about which source wins when guidance conflicts,

00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:51.003
how stale material is handled,

00:00:51.003 --> 00:00:55.336
and when the system should decline to answer or ask for review.

00:00:55.336 --> 00:01:01.112
Good private RAG design makes source visibility part of the user experience and the operating model.

00:01:01.112 --> 00:01:05.805
Users and reviewers should be able to understand where an answer came from,

00:01:05.805 --> 00:01:07.610
why those sources were selected,

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:11.220
and whether the content is current enough for the task.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.831
The value of private RAG is not just better answers.

00:01:14.831 --> 00:01:16.275
It is accountable answers.

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:19.163
The system is strongest when retrieval, permissions, provenance,

00:01:19.163 --> 00:01:23.495
and lifecycle controls are designed together so users can trust the answer

00:01:23.495 --> 00:01:25.300
and the boundary behind it.
